package server

const mcpWorkspaceSecurityPolicy = "GET /workspace/security discovers safe versioned metadata for the connected browser's actual backend: type:workspace-security,schemaVersion:1,mode:encrypted|legacy,state,logicalSchemaVersion, optional vaultSchemaVersion:1 and cipher:AES-256-GCM, requiresHumanUnlock, programmaticUnlock:false, programmaticLock and requestsRenewIdleTimeout:false and contentRequiresUnlock. It exposes no vault IDs, keys, salts, credentials, expiry timestamps, grants or private records and may be read while locked. Static GET /api/v1/health reports bridge connectivity, not browser lock status. Encrypted private commands use the same authoritative UI/API/MCP storage boundary and require a human-unlocked browser plus the existing access grant. Only an already authorized open socket is retained for restricted control; cold locked startup never connects and a closed control socket is not reconnected. Same-workspace routing prefers an available content peer, without retrying dispatched writes. A connected locked command returns structured status 423 with code WORKSPACE_LOCKED; disconnected/unavailable workspaces remain 503. After each encrypted-session unlock access starts Off; the human must choose a fresh Read only or Read + write grant in Settings. POST /workspace/lock accepts only an empty object or no arguments. An unlocked encrypted browser requires a fresh Read + write grant, saves pending edits, then intentionally revokes the session and returns safe status. Save failure does not silently discard edits. A durable revision fence rejects concurrent grant or saved-data changes with 409 without invalidating local keys; inspect current state before a fresh request. Already-locked retained control returns idempotent status without another revocation; after unlock its old connection cannot lock or access content until a fresh human grant. Explicit Off disconnects even when a previous grant has already been revoked. No password, recovery, unlock or session-policy control endpoint exists; /settings/vault-* writes are rejected. Requests do not renew idle timeout. Lock cancels jobs and revokes originating operations, even after a later unlock. Do not ask an agent for the password or recovery key. Documentation remains discoverable without any connected/unlocked browser. Explicit authorized AI/API requests and diagram exports expose readable content; GET /workspace/export returns readable semantic data, not the browser's encrypted backup download. Downloaded encrypted backups keep their own credentials after a live password change. This is local browser protection, without mandatory backend/SSO or security certification claims."
